---
description: Use bb-code context and finish active bb-code runs
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of every coding request, call `bb_context` exactly once with the user's request and any relevant paths before planning or editing. A normal result, including "No relevant bb-code context was found," is successful; retry only when Cursor reports that the MCP call itself failed. For a focused follow-up lookup, pass the active `runId` returned by the initial call. Treat returned commitments as constraints, beliefs as fallible context, and intents as goals. Report raw registered statement IDs through `contextEffects` when they materially affect the work.

The `bb_context` result includes the active run ID when its request exactly matches the current user prompt. If the owner's current request changes or reverses a retrieved commitment, call `bb_propose_update` with revise, supersede, or retire before editing affected paths. Before your final response after tool-assisted work, call `bb_finish_run` with that run ID and reconcile every registered commitment. Propose only durable knowledge likely to change future work; repository knowledge mode resolves proposals. If there is no useful durable learning, provide a specific `noDurableLearningReason`.
